  "slug": "spin-altermagnetism-d7e3",
  "summary": "Five preprints link symmetry-defined orders to predicted Hall and spin-transport responses, with electric-field or stacking tunability in several cases.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is theory deriving measurable transport responses from symmetry-defined order. For odd-parity magnets, charge-spin selection rules and temporal-spectral separation are proposed as general transport signatures. In monolayer H-phase MoS2, an orbital exchange field is shown to induce an intrinsic anomalous Hall conductivity without spin magnetism or spin-orbit coupling. Twisted bilayer NiPS3 is predicted to host p-wave spin textures that a perpendicular electric field reorients. Sliding antiferroelectric four-layer MoS2 is predicted to show a quantum-metric-driven nonlinear valley Hall effect, and axial ferrons in uniaxial ferroelectrics to show thermal and angular-momentum Hall effects. New here is the emphasis on orbital-only mechanisms and on electric-field or stacking tunability. All five items are preprints, with predictions from theory and first-principles calculations.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-27"
}
